# Architecture-First Gate

- Read `docs/00-governance/CURRENT_PHASE.md` before changing this project.
- While `IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZED` is `false`, work only on architecture
  research, Markdown artifacts, reviews, registers, and approved Cursor controls.
- Do not create application code, executable schemas/migrations, API/UI
  implementation, package manifests, dependency installs, CI/CD, Docker, or
  deployment implementation.
- Node.js + TypeScript is confirmed; frameworks and packages are not confirmed
  unless an accepted ADR says so.
- Never resolve material business or architecture ambiguity silently. Add or
  update an `OQ-*`, `ASM-*`, `RISK-*`, `FIND-*`, or `ADR-*` record.
- Use canonical terms and ownership from `docs/00-governance/registers/`; phase
  documents link to them instead of redefining them.
- Every phase requires self-check, independent review, reconciliation, explicit
  user approval, and a checkpoint before the next phase.
- Git staging/commit requires a short-lived, human-created protected checkpoint
  marker referencing the approved phase manifest and exact Git commands.
- Discussion, a completed draft, or an AI recommendation does not authorize
  implementation.
- A future implementation unlock must reference the exact approved baseline and
  narrowly authorized paths. Its absence means implementation remains locked.
